{
  "board": { "name": "Marketing Agency", "color": "#7C5CFF" },
  "columns": [
    {
      "name": "Research",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Validate demo quality bar against Durable/B12/Framer",
          "label": "research",
          "body": "Manually generate 3 sample demos (dentist, restaurant, gym) with Claude Sonnet 4.6 structured output and compare side-by-side to what Durable (~$12/mo), B12 (~$42/mo) and Framer AI produce for the same inputs. **Goal:** confirm our per-vertical designed templates beat generic AI-builder output enough to justify the pitch. **Deliverable:** a scored rubric (design, copy, on-brandness, perf) + screenshots. If we can't clearly beat Durable, the wedge is weak — revisit."
        },
        {
          "title": "Cost model per demo at 1k / 10k prospects",
          "label": "research",
          "body": "Build a spreadsheet for marginal cost/demo: scrape (Playwright free vs Firecrawl ~$0.0008/page + separate /extract token bill), LLM gen (~$0.10–0.60/site Sonnet, Haiku for extraction, Opus only for hero), deploy (Nxeon disk+cert ≈ free), screenshots. Model Anthropic **Batch API** (~50% off) and Firecrawl tier breakpoints (Free 1k → Hobby $16 → Standard $83). **Output:** cost/demo and monthly burn at 1k and 10k demos, plus a per-prospect spend cap recommendation."
        },
        {
          "title": "Legal review: nominative fair use + logo/brand in unsolicited demos",
          "label": "legal",
          "body": "Get written guidance (or a lawyer sign-off) on the plan in architecture.md §11. Confirm: (1) plain-text business name = defensible nominative fair use; (2) re-hosting their actual **logo/exact font/full palette** is the risk line — default to name-in-type + neutral/generated mark + inspired-by palette; (3) required disclaimer wording; (4) copyright — we rewrite copy + use licensed/generated imagery, never republish theirs. Sources: INTA, Chase Law, Nolo, Davis+Gilbert (see architecture.md §12). **Output:** an approved do/don't checklist the generator must enforce in code."
        },
        {
          "title": "Anti-spam & deliverability boundaries with Cold Email Engine",
          "label": "research",
          "body": "Define the contract split: Cold Email Engine owns sending + CAN-SPAM/GDPR/PECR/CASL compliance; we own demo hosting + opt-out/takedown + suppression list. **Research:** does hosting many auto-gen sites on a shared IP hurt Google Safe Browsing / sender reputation? Decide to (a) isolate the demo domain+IP from production customer IPs and from the sending domain, and (b) noindex+robots-disallow all demos. **Output:** an integration spec (webhook payload `demo.ready`, event callbacks open/click/claim) + a reputation-isolation plan."
        },
        {
          "title": "Scraping legality & anti-bot resilience",
          "label": "research",
          "body": "Decide the scraping policy: respect robots.txt/ToS, public pages only, throttled, identified UA, allow/deny list + kill switch. Test Playwright vs Firecrawl on 20 real-vertical sites for anti-bot blocking and extraction quality (logo, colors, services, hours, reviews). Define the **no-site fallback**: generate purely from Google Places data (a business with no site is a *better* target). **Output:** scraping runbook + when to escalate Playwright→Firecrawl→Places-only."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Ideas",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Before/after slider in outreach + on the demo",
          "label": "idea",
          "body": "Capture a full-page screenshot of the prospect's current site and render an interactive before/after slider (or a static side-by-side image) embedded in the outreach email and at the top of the claim page. High emotional impact — they *see* the upgrade. Reuse Playwright/Firecrawl screenshots already captured in the pipeline."
        },
        {
          "title": "Personalized claim page ('make it yours')",
          "label": "idea",
          "body": "Every demo link resolves to `sub.demos.<domain>` with a discreet claim CTA bar: 'Love it? Book a call / Get this live in 48h.' Claim URL carries a signed token → fires DemoEvent(CLAIMED) → auto-creates a Deal in the pipeline. This is the warm-lead capture that turns a cold click into a booked call."
        },
        {
          "title": "Learn which templates/designs convert (feedback loop)",
          "label": "idea",
          "body": "Track funnel per template/vertical: sent → opened → clicked → claimed → won. Feed win-rate back into template selection and A/B new template variants. Over time the engine picks the highest-converting design per vertico automatically. Requires the analytics dashboard (Later)."
        },
        {
          "title": "White-label for sub-agencies",
          "label": "idea",
          "body": "Multi-tenant mode: other agencies run their own demo campaigns under their brand on our engine, their own demo domain, their own API keys, isolated data. Revenue = SaaS seats. Needs the Tenant/Setting model and strict data isolation. Phase 3+ once the single-tenant loop converts."
        },
        {
          "title": "Generated hero imagery per vertical",
          "label": "idea",
          "body": "Instead of stock, generate on-brand hero/section imagery (SDXL/Flux via Replicate, or licensed Unsplash/Pexels). Avoids the legal problem of reusing the prospect's photos and makes demos look bespoke. Optional cost — gate behind a per-demo flag."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Backlog",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Agency CRM pipeline (reuse Nxeon Board)",
          "label": "backlog",
          "body": "Full deal pipeline: Lead → Demo Sent → Opened → Replied → Call → Won → Onboarding → Live → Retainer. Reuse the existing Nxeon Board (`/admin/board`) primitives rather than building a new kanban. Models: Deal, Proposal, Client. A claim/reply event auto-advances the card. Phase 3."
        },
        {
          "title": "Proposals & contracts (e-sign)",
          "label": "backlog",
          "body": "Generate a proposal from the won deal + demo (scope, package, price from §pricing), send for e-signature, track signed. Consider a lightweight e-sign integration or a hosted proposal page + click-to-accept. Feeds billing setup on signature."
        },
        {
          "title": "Billing & retainers via Nxeon Stripe",
          "label": "backlog",
          "body": "Reuse Nxeon's existing Stripe integration for won-client billing: one-time build fee + monthly retainer subscription. Map packages (see pricing card) to Stripe products/prices. Client dashboard shows invoices. Phase 3."
        },
        {
          "title": "Handoff: promote demo → real owned site",
          "label": "backlog",
          "body": "When a client signs, promote the demo IR to a real, owned site: create a Nxeon shared-hosting account, deploy the (now editable) site, attach their custom domain + real SSL, migrate content, remove the disclaimer/noindex. Reuses the shared-hosting provisioner + migration engine. This is the 'agency delivers' moment."
        },
        {
          "title": "Pricing & packaging definition",
          "label": "backlog",
          "body": "Define productized tiers using 2026 market data: one-off build $2.5k–$10k+; monthly retainer $1k–$3k (solo/boutique) up to $5k–$15k (mid); subscription-agency model $4.7k–$9.9k/mo (assembly.com, manypixels, taskip sources in architecture.md §12). Propose 3 packages (Starter/Growth/Full-Service) mapping to build fee + retainer + what's included (hosting, edits, SEO). **Output:** a pricing page + Stripe price IDs."
        },
        {
          "title": "Analytics dashboard (funnel + cohort)",
          "label": "backlog",
          "body": "Admin dashboard: demos generated, sent, open/click/claim/won rates by vertical/template/campaign, cost per demo, cost per won client, teardown/expiry counts. Powers the 'learn which designs convert' loop. Build after volume exists (Phase 2/3)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Phase 1",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Define Site IR schema + JSON Schema validation",
          "label": "phase1",
          "body": "Design the **Site Intermediate Representation**: `page → sections[] → blocks[]` with typed props (hero, servicesGrid, about, testimonials, gallery, bookingCTA, map, faq, footer) + theme tokens (colors, fonts, radius). Emit it from Claude via **structured output / tool-use**, NOT raw HTML (2026 best practice — Outlines/tool-use). Write the JSON Schema and a validator that rejects/repairs invalid IR before render. **This is the backbone every other Phase 1 card depends on.**"
        },
        {
          "title": "Build first vertical template (dentist)",
          "label": "phase1",
          "body": "One production-grade vertical template: a `sectionCatalog` of React components (hero, services, about, testimonials, booking CTA, map, FAQ, footer) + `themeTokens` + `promptPack` (vertical-specific copy guidance) + curated hero imagery set. Must render from IR deterministically. Design to Nxeon's design system (`components/ui/`, `globals.css`). Bar: visibly beats Durable/B12 for a dentist."
        },
        {
          "title": "Scrape + brand-extract → BrandProfile",
          "label": "phase1",
          "body": "Pipeline step: fetch current site (Playwright MVP), capture HTML + full-page screenshot, extract **logo, palette, fonts, headings, services, hours, address, phone, review snippets** (Brandfetch API for logo/colors, or Firecrawl /extract). Store `BrandProfile`. Respect robots/ToS + rate-limit. Implement the **no-site fallback** (generate from Google Places data only). Env: `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`, `BRANDFETCH_API_KEY`, `GOOGLE_PLACES_KEY`."
        },
        {
          "title": "Claude generation: plan → IR",
          "label": "phase1",
          "body": "Given BrandProfile + vertical template `sectionCatalog`, call Claude Sonnet 4.6 with structured output to: choose sections, write on-brand copy, map extracted colors→theme tokens (with **contrast/accessibility guardrails**), pick imagery. Use Haiku for the cheap classify/summarize pre-step. Validate output against the IR JSON Schema; repair on failure. Cap tokens/spend per prospect. Env: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`."
        },
        {
          "title": "Deterministic renderer: IR → static HTML export",
          "label": "phase1",
          "body": "Map validated IR + template components + theme tokens → **static HTML/CSS export** (cheapest, no runtime). Enforce the legal guardrails from the legal card: name-in-type not verbatim logo (unless consent flag), inspired-by palette, **mandatory disclaimer** ('Unofficial concept redesign by <Agency>, not affiliated/endorsed'), plus `noindex` + robots-disallow meta. Inject the claim CTA bar."
        },
        {
          "title": "QA gate before a demo can be sent",
          "label": "phase1",
          "body": "Automated checks that block deploy/send on failure: valid HTML, Lighthouse/perf threshold, no broken links, color contrast, profanity/hallucinated-claims scan, **disclaimer + noindex present**. Route borderline demos to a **human-approve queue** (Phase 1 = human-in-loop). Only APPROVED demos advance to deploy."
        },
        {
          "title": "Demo deploy provisioner on Nxeon (subdomain + SNI SSL)",
          "label": "phase1",
          "body": "Add an `agency-demo` provisioner reusing shared-hosting infra: (1) one-time wildcard `*.demos.<domain>` A record via Namecheap lib → HostingNode IP; (2) per-demo name-based nginx vhost `sub.demos.<domain>` → static dir; (3) drop exported HTML; (4) reuse the existing **SSL sweep** (certbot-webroot, per-domain SNI cert) once DNS resolves; (5) reuse the catch-all default vhost for safety. NO new hosting vendor. Model as worker jobs (DEPLOY). Isolate the demo IP from production customer IPs."
        },
        {
          "title": "Worker job queue + Demo state machine",
          "label": "phase1",
          "body": "Mirror Nxeon's HostingTask/worker-tick pattern. Jobs: SCRAPE, GENERATE, RENDER, QA, DEPLOY, SCREENSHOT, NOTIFY_OUTREACH — each status-driven with retries. Demo status: `QUEUED→SCRAPING→GENERATING→RENDERING→DEPLOYING→LIVE→(SENT→OPENED→CLAIMED)/FAILED/EXPIRED`. Self-completing so a batch of prospects runs unattended. Feature-flag `ENABLE_AGENCY=1`, inert until reviewed (shared-hosting pattern)."
        },
        {
          "title": "Cold Email Engine handoff + event tracking",
          "label": "phase1",
          "body": "On demo LIVE + approved, emit `demo.ready` webhook to the Cold Email Engine with `{prospect, deployUrl, beforeAfterImg, claimUrl}`. **We do NOT send email.** Host the claim redirect + tracking pixel; receive/emit open/click/claim callbacks → DemoEvent. Stub the Cold Email Engine with a mock endpoint if it isn't ready yet so the loop is testable end-to-end."
        },
        {
          "title": "Admin demo list + prospect import (CSV/Places)",
          "label": "phase1",
          "body": "Minimal admin surface at `/admin/agency`: import prospects (CSV or Google Places pull), assign vertical (heuristic + LLM classifier fallback), see the demo pipeline status per prospect, preview/approve demos, view deploy URL + events. Reuse `Shell.tsx` + `components/ui/`. Additive `Agency*` Prisma models — never touch VPS/hosting models."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Later",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Expand to 5–10 verticals + template library tooling",
          "label": "later",
          "body": "Add restaurant, gym, law firm, salon, HVAC, med-spa, auto shop templates. Build internal tooling to author a vertical (sectionCatalog + themeTokens + promptPack + imagery) quickly so adding a vertical is hours not weeks. Phase 2."
        },
        {
          "title": "Batch generation + auto-approve for high-confidence",
          "label": "later",
          "body": "Use Anthropic **Batch API** (~50% cheaper) for bulk demo generation. Add a confidence score to the QA gate so high-confidence demos auto-approve and only borderline ones need a human. Enables 1k–10k demo campaigns. Phase 2."
        },
        {
          "title": "Wildcard cert via DNS-01 (high demo volume)",
          "label": "later",
          "body": "If per-host SNI cert issuance becomes a bottleneck at volume, switch to a single wildcard `*.demos.<domain>` cert via **DNS-01** challenge (Namecheap creds already enable it; Traefik/certbot DNS plugin). Then every subdomain is instantly TLS-covered with no per-demo cert. Evaluate vs SNI once >~500 concurrent demos."
        },
        {
          "title": "Multi-tenant + white-label platform",
          "label": "later",
          "body": "Turn the engine into a SaaS other agencies rent: Tenant/Setting model, per-tenant API keys + demo domain + isolated data, seat billing. Requires hardened data isolation (like shared-hosting isolation discipline). Phase 3+."
        },
        {
          "title": "Standalone app packaging (dev box)",
          "label": "later",
          "body": "Package the core (pipeline, IR, renderer, template library, provisioner + outreach interfaces) as `agency-core` shared between the Nxeon add-on and a standalone `agency.<domain>` Next app + own Postgres on dev box 51.79.226.215. Standalone deploy adapter talks to a Nxeon HostingNode over the same provisioner contract. Own auth/billing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Done",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Product architecture + build plan documented",
          "label": "done",
          "body": "Wrote architecture.md: product overview, competitor matrix (Durable/B12/10Web/Framer/v0 + spec-site plays), exact external APIs + pricing (Anthropic, Firecrawl, Brandfetch, Places, Unsplash) with links, tech stack, data model, 11-step generation+deploy pipeline, standalone vs Nxeon-add-on plan, 4 phases, risks, and mandatory legal/ethical/compliance section. Cited sources."
        },
        {
          "title": "Confirmed Nxeon infra reuse for demo hosting",
          "label": "done",
          "body": "Verified from Nxeon shared-hosting build that demo deploy = the cheapest shared-hosting case: name-based nginx vhosts routing by Host header, per-domain SNI SSL via the existing certbot-webroot sweep, a worker task queue to copy, Namecheap DNS for the wildcard A record, and a catch-all vhost for safety. **Conclusion: no new hosting vendor needed; marginal deploy cost ≈ disk + a cert.**"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
